  "title": "Kaplansky's Conjectures",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A set of conjectures about group rings: (1) Zero divisor conjecture: If $G$ is a torsion-free group and $K$ is a field, then $K[G]$ has no zero divisors. (2) Idempotent conjecture: The only idempotents in $K[G]$ are 0 and 1. (3) Unit conjecture: The only units in $\\mathbb{Z}[G]$ are of the form $\\pm g$ for $g \\in G$.",
